  "scope": "The complete six-measure equality of Federer 3.2.26, pp. 261\u2013262, on every finite (H^m,m)-rectifiable W in R^n, m<=n, without W measurability. Spherical, Hausdorff, exterior-diameter, Gross, convex integral-geometric and integral-geometric measure agree for every exponent 1<=t<=infinity. The existing natural-degree interfaces also retain degree zero.",
  "proof_route": "Prove S=H by upper density, 2.10.19(3), rough null control and a threshold limit through true measure-hull test laws. Prove Q_t<=H using the actual normalized tangent unit disc, near-optimal open convex neighbourhoods, actual differentiability and inverse chart bounds, positive affine similarity scaling, finite-measure Vitali covering, cutoff cost and a (1+delta)^2 squeeze. Neighbourhoods depend on the actual tangent plane and have scaled diameter at most 3r instead of the printed tube diameter 2r; smaller cutoff radii compensate. Sum disjoint compact charts and pass through a true rectifiable Borel hull for arbitrary W. Prove H<=I_t using exact small Borel partitions of the 3.2.25 orientation, actual restricted tangent-cone equality, projection contraction, the corrected 3.2.20 area identity and actual fibre multiplicity. Probability Minkowski and beta normalization give an additive uniform-error estimate; countable sums and finite mass remove the error. For arbitrary W intersect its rectifiable Hausdorff hull with an equal-I_t Borel cover and use monotonicity, without declaring a hull difference null. Finish through the independently proved chain I_infinity<=G<=T<=H, avoiding forward dependencies in the complete 2.10.6 summary.",
  "erratum_correction": "Erratum p. 5: book p. 261 line 22 refers to 2.10.5, line 29 uses x-w, and p. 262 line 14 refers to 3.2.20.",
